# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# THE CORPUS IS EVIDENCE. Do not let git touch a byte of it.
#
# `* text=auto` above normalises line endings on anything git decides is text,
# and captures.jsonl is text by that test. Normalisation is harmless for source
# and wrong here: this archive's central rule is that every figure traces back
# to bytes actually retrieved from a source, and bytes git rewrote on checkout
# are no longer those bytes. Parsers are verified against this corpus, so a CRLF
# appearing on one platform and not another is a test that passes on one machine
# and fails on the other for a reason nobody will find quickly.
data/captures.jsonl -text
data/blobs/** binary

# The derived records, for the same reason one step removed. These are the only
# surviving trace of three documents that are not published, and they are what a
# build server reads in place of them. Nothing downstream cares about a line
# ending — but the whole point of storing them is that this machine and a runner
# produce the same site.json from the same bytes, and `text=auto` would hand the
# two of them different bytes.
data/derived/*.json -text

# The captain's roster book and the stats workbook build:data depends on.
*.xlsx binary
